>> title: Corned Beef Hash
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: corned beef, potatoes, breakfast, skillet, leftovers
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: hash, diner hash, corned beef hash, red flannel hash
>> pairs-with: corned-beef
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: simmer the diced potato 8 min, drain
>> step.2: sweat 5 min, until soft and pale
>> step.3: fold the three together, no mashing
>> step.4: press flat, leave it alone 8 min, turn in slabs

Simmer @Yukon Gold potatoes{1%lb}(450 g; peeled, in 1/2-in dice) in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) with @kosher salt{2%tsp}(12 g) ~simmer{8%min}, until barely tender, then drain them and let the steam go.

Sweat @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced small) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(30 g) in a #cast-iron skillet{} over medium heat ~fry{5%min}.

Fold @&(~2)drained potatoes{} and @corned beef{12%oz}(340 g; chopped by hand, not ground) into @&(~1)sweated onion{}.

Press @&(~1)hash{} flat, season with @coarse black pepper{1%tsp}(2 g) and @Worcestershire sauce{2%tsp}(10 mL), and leave it alone over medium heat ~fry{8%min}, then turn it in slabs rather than stirring.
